Under our guidance, duty on a duty-paid release is due **at the point of release, before the cask leaves bond**. Spirits duty is charged on the litres of pure alcohol in the cask.

For cask 102, the register shows:
- Craigtarry single malt in a first-fill bourbon barrel, filled 11 March 2014
- 182 bulk litres at 57.8% ABV
- Currently in bond in Warehouse 2, Craigtarry bond

The guidance doesn't give a payment deadline or a duty rate, so I can't say more than that duty must be paid before the cask is released from bond. For the exact amount and how to arrange payment, please contact the distillery's bond team directly.
